{
 "slot": 57,
 "name": "Eight Channels",
 "group": "other",
 "notes": {
  "sound": "Eight mono lines, one per MIDI channel 1-8, and no two alike: the channel number shapes the sound, from a dark, sustained, sliding bass on channel 1 to a bright, barking, snappy pluck with no glide on channel 8, the channels between grading from one to the other (a saw with a pulse an octave down throughout). Each channel has its own bend, pressure and CC 74 brightness. Made for sequencers that drive eight lines.",
  "shows": "The 8ch layer mode; the voice-number source (voice = channel here) into cutoff, the filter envelope's amount, the sustains, decays and glide; Timbre (CC 74) and aftertouch per voice."
 },
